2567	340	340	2004-06-24T00:00:00+00:00 University-of-Cambridge-ESOL-2004	0	{"id": ["None", "340"], "added": ["None", "2026-05-31 13:23:27.181646"], "notes": ["None", "documents.Note.None"], "owner": ["None", "None"], "title": ["None", "University-of-Cambridge-ESOL-2004"], "content": ["None", "UNIVERSITY of CAMBRIDGE Hi\\n\\nESOL Examinations teal\\n\\nEnglish for Speakers of Other Languages\\n\\nEntry Level Certificate in English (ESOL)* -\\n\\n*\\na”\\n\\n4\\n\\nH\\nS3 ip aHNoAS\\n\\nWRis 4a ke ve id\\n\\n‘2!\\n\\nPAT ey\\n\\nBEGUHE 4 aI SS FS ECUHEFSECU\\n\\nHNDAS Ke\\n\\nSpicer,\\n\\naH RE *BYNOSS * SECURE ¥ OOM\\nAMON ACE CURE ABHNOAG ASUANIAC\\n\\n*\\n3\\n4\\n\\nFore et\\n\\nve cs\\nASE CHIE IS SRDS SFCURE 4SECURE\\n\\nOo DRESS\\n\\n4 SECUHE 4 SE CUE\\n\\nSHOWS k GRC ANAS A BHATDNSS x\\n\\nSidNDaS * SECURE *+3unN\\n\\nMAY (A) 2004\\n\\nMUNIGH . pa\\n045DE6106241 Ww : / Wr A QNWnm™ at\\n\\n* 400/2031/7 Michael Milanovic oan\\nChief Executive Aen\\n\\nREM SECURE 4 aI\\n\\nrR\\nc\\n\\npeer ne weeny\\n| ee. ruse\\nQ C A —— , CummcuLs 6 ycue\\n\\n* aaa Guarding standards Rewarding Leaming\\n\\nCertificate Number 0011765952\\n\\n—\\n\\n045DE6106241 | | THOMAS VERHULSDONK\\n\\nStatement of Results\\n\\nENGLISH FOR SPEAKERS OF OTHER LANGUAGES. | Session\\n\\nPreliminary English Test : | pein\\nReference No. Candidate Name\\n\\nTo be quoted on ail Place of Entry\\n\\ndei\\ncorrespondence MUNICH\\nQualification Result\\nPRELIMINARY ENGLISH TEST PASS\\nCandidate Profile\\nSco ae Listening\\n| Writing\\n= Speaking\\nBorderline\\nWeak\\nExplanatory Notes\\n\\n1. A statement of results is not a certificate, and is issued to every candidate. Certificates will be issued later to successful candidates.\\n2. Cambridge ESOL reserves the right to amend the information given before the issue of certificates to successful candidates.\\n\\nGENERAL DESCRIPTION OF THE PRELIMINARY ENGLISH TEST (PET)\\nPET is a general proficiency examination at Level B1 in the Council of Europe Common European Framework. It is at Entry Level 3 in the UK\\n\\nNational Qualifications Framework.\\n\\nCouncil of Europe Level Examination\\nResearch has shown that typical candidates at Level B1 can:\\n\\nC2 CPE - express opinions on abstract/cultural matters in a limited way or offer advice within\\nC1 CAE a known area, and understand instructions or public announcements.\\n\\nB2 FCE - understand routine information and articles, and the general meaning of\\n\\nB1 PET non-routine information, within a familiar area.\\n\\nA2 KET - write letters or make notes on familiar or predictable matters.\\n\\nINTERPRETATION OF OVERALL GRADES\\n\\nThe percentage of marks needed to achieve each grade may vary from session to session depending on the precise difficulty of the individual papers\\nwhich make up the particular examination. The approximate ranges of percentages for each grade at PET are typically as follows:\\n\\nPassing Pass withMerit 85% and above Absent Candidates\\nGrades Pass 70% to 84% Grade X indicates that a candidate was absent from part of the examination.\\nGrade Z indicates that the candidate was absent from all parts of the examination.\\nFalling Narrow Fail 65% to 69% PENDING indicates that a result cannot be issued at present, but will follow in due course.\\nGrades Fail 64% and below\\n\\nThe grades above do not correspond to the shaded bands on the candidate profile.\\naii ae eee ee\\n\\na ae of CAMBRIDGE\\ny ESOL Examinations\\n\\n24/06/04"], "created": ["None", "2004-06-24 00:00:00+00:00"], "checksum": ["None", "cc261764aa8129f78a9d4f99c2bbf53c"], "mime_type": ["None", "application/pdf"], "deleted_at": ["None", "None"], "page_count": ["None", "2"], "restored_at": ["None", "None"], "share_links": ["None", "documents.ShareLink.None"], "storage_path": ["None", "None"], "storage_type": ["None", "unencrypted"], "correspondent": ["None", "None"], "custom_fields": ["None", "documents.CustomFieldInstance.None"], "document_type": ["None", "None"], "workflow_runs